<title>USA: San Francisco city plans Asia trade mission.</title>
<headline>San Francisco city plans Asia trade mission.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>San Francisco Mayor Willie Brown will lead a city delegation on a two-week trade mission to China, Hong Kong and Taiwan at the end of March, his office said on Monday.</p>
<p>Thirty delegates are expected to accompany Brown on the trade mission, including two San Francisco supervisors and several local businessmen.</p>
<p>Brown said the delegation would leave March 30, and would visit Shanghai, Beijing, Hong Kong and Taipei.</p>
<p>During the visit, Brown plans to promote business opportunities in San Francisco, his office said.</p>
<p>Last year, Brown led a trade mission to Paris.</p>
</text>
